{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1462889691,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDY1NTgxODkwMg=="},"added":["severity-normal"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1462973111,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIxODQ1NzkxOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/432#issuecomment-218457918"},"message":"We should have a dedicated publishing \"mode\" for this. My internal label for this one is \"publish as is\" -- meaning we aim to create a more-or-less duplicate of a local dataset (with subdatasets) at a remote location. The difference from a plain rsync is that the result should be a fully connected git repository.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1462973122,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDY1NzE1NjUxNQ=="},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1462973929,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIxODQ2MTU5Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/432#issuecomment-218461596"},"message":"On Wed, 11 May 2016, Michael Hanke wrote:\n\n\u003e    We should have a dedicated publishing \"mode\" for this. My internal label\n\u003e    for this one is \"publish as is\" -- meaning we aim to create a more-or-less\n\u003e    duplicate of a local dataset (with subdatasets) at a remote location. The\n\u003e    difference from a plain rsync is that the result should be a fully\n\u003e    connected git repository.\n\nbut as is means to me that remote location should be as potent annex as\nlocal one.  All annexes should have different uuid's, so something\nshould init it on the remote end.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1462973982,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIxODQ2MTgzNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/432#issuecomment-218461837"},"message":"Yes, that is implied.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1464098908,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMTI4MjI5NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/432#issuecomment-221282294"},"message":"Not sure, whether this should be a part of `datalad publish` command, since this functionality is depending on the kind of target you want to publish to. (needs SSH)\nSo, may be there should be some \"post-publish\" command instead?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1464099118,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMTI4MzQ4NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/432#issuecomment-221283485"},"message":"Alternatively, we may provide a post-update hook for the target via `create-publication-target`, that checks for a git-annex branch, that was created by a push? Something like this ....?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1464099579,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMTI4NTk5OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/432#issuecomment-221285998"},"message":"that is why I kept `*` in the name -- choose the most appropriate point ;)  But I don't think hooks (intended for re-doing things on each push/pull/whatever) is really worth messing with for this -- this is as far as I see it a one time action to perform.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cba82ee60a840e58af2a6904e43bb376b414fe4e"},"timestamp":1470674044,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50NzQ4NjQ5ODk0"},"status":2}]}